<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade-May 17.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade-May 17.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended May 17</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE   % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				(RS MLN)</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>State Bank	   305	   0.49     524250  159.90    8.38</p>
<p>Colgate		295	   0.48     159750   47.13    8.48</p>
<p>Bajaj Auto	   870	   1.42	49700   43.24    8.51</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    215	   0.35     196900   42.33    8.49</p>
<p>Sterlite	     270	   0.44     107600   29.05    8.50</p>
<p>ACC		   1170	   1.94	24250   28.37    8.65</p>
<p>IPCL		   139	   0.36     182800   25.41   13.50</p>
<p>Castrol		440	   0.72	54500   23.98    8.53</p>
<p>Century Textiles  1890	   3.07	11600   21.92    8.47</p>
<p>Arvind Mills	 131	   0.22     157930   20.69    8.76</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 8.32 percent on an annualised basis against 10.03 % in the previous carry forward account ended May 10</p>
